# Files this repo deliberately does NOT carry from its template.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. Every repo in this tree merges from a `stem` remote. A file
# that a descendant has deleted is not a settled decision as far as git is
# concerned: the next time the template TOUCHES that file, the cascade stops
# with a modify/delete conflict, and whoever is running it has to work out from
# scratch whether the deletion was deliberate.
#
# Listing the path here does not change what git does - the conflict still
# happens - but it makes the answer a lookup instead of an excavation, and
# `scripts/apply-omissions.sh` turns the resolution into one command.
#
# FORMAT. One path per line, relative to the repo root. `#` starts a comment.
# Give every entry a reason: the next person's question is never "which file",
# it is "why", and an unexplained list is how a deletion outlives the reason for
# it and becomes cargo cult. A DIRECTORY entry covers everything under it, which
# is usually what you want: a whole replaced directory rather than forty files.
#
# THREE GUARDS, all pointing different ways:
#
#   web/test/offshoot-omissions.test.ts   every LISTED path is still absent
#   scripts/check-omissions.mjs           every ABSENT path is listed (needs the stem)
#   scripts/apply-omissions.sh            re-drop them all, and run both checks
#
# ENTRIES ARE STEM-RELATIVE: what belongs in a repo's list is what IT drops from
# ITS stem. A descendant must not copy this file's entries down, and this one has
# none to copy.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS TEMPLATE OMITS NOTHING, and unlike the last file in this tree to say that,
# it has been CHECKED: `node scripts/check-omissions.mjs` against
# `template-svelte-tailwind` reports zero paths dropped. The sentence is allowed to
# stay only because a command backs it.
#
# THE MACHINERY IS HERE ANYWAY, ON PURPOSE. Two repos built from this template drop
# things and had no way to record it: `ronan-eth` drops the two sample posts, and
# `conquest-website-2` drops those plus the whole `routes/blog/` tree. An ancestor is
# the distribution point for shared machinery even when it has nothing of its own to
# guard - the alternative is a copy of the same three files in each descendant, which
# is the divergence-by-copy this tree keeps paying for.
#
# It came from jolly-roger, the other branch of this tree, where the same audit found
# every one of five lists incomplete and one cascade had already paid for it. The two
# copies are identical today; the single home for them is `template-svelte`, the root,
# and moving them there is a tree-wide cascade nobody has paid for yet. Until someone
# does, a change to one of these three files belongs in both.
